---
/**
 * ServiceHero — the first screen of the v2.0 doorway. PAPER register only.
 *
 * WHAT CHANGED FROM THE v1.1 HERO, AND WHY (CG2 final E rulings, 2026-08-26 15:59, items 3 and 7). v1.1 organised the
 * category around CAN vs MAY. v2.0 organises it around the LEGITIMACY OF A SERVICE and demotes
 * servability from the thesis to a gate inside it — "Service is the mission. Servability is a
 * governing gate." So the old proposition ("What can be computed is not yet what may be served") is
 * not merely reworded: it is no longer the organising claim. It returns in §The servability gap, in
 * the record's own words, and the preserved v1.1 hero keeps it at
 * /history/analytical-governance-v1-1.
 *
 * THE H1 IS RULED, AND THE WORD "CORRECT" IS DELIBERATELY ABSENT (Huayin, final E rulings,
 * 2026-08-26 15:59, item 3). An earlier draft read "A correct number can still fail the service." It was refused for a
 * precise reason: a result can be correct RELATIVE TO an arithmetic operation, a query, a
 * derivation, or a particular analytical object, while in the wider sense "the correct answer"
 * already includes whether it answers the right question under the required grounds. Calling the
 * number correct and then saying it failed equivocates on the word. The ruled H1 uses the paper's own
 * two terms instead, whose definitions are typed on this page:
 *
 *     Result — the product of the governed analytical process.
 *     Answer — a result served as responsive to the request.
 *
 * THE CRITERION BAND is v2.0-grounded. The v1.1 aphorism "If it cannot refuse, it is not governed"
 * is NOT inherited: v2.0 does not state it, and item 9 of the final E rulings forbids carrying retired material into
 * current authority. What v2.0 does state is the §12 requirement (a servability gate capable of
 * withholding or qualifying analytical permission) and the §5 line (refusal is evidence that
 * analytical permission is real). Both are used, in that order.
 *
 * The signpost is REGISTRY-DERIVED. No version, date or DOI is typed on this page.
 */
import { citation, longDate } from '../../data/publications';

const paper = citation('w-analytical-governance');
---

<section class="ag-hero ds ds-paper ds-section" id="service" aria-labelledby="ag-thesis">
  <div class="ds-measure-wide">
    <p class="ds-label">Analytical Governance</p>

    <h1 id="ag-thesis" class="proposition">
      Producing a result is not the same as serving an answer.
    </h1>

    <p class="organizing">
      Analytical Governance is the discipline governing the <em>legitimacy of the analytical
      service</em>: the user&rsquo;s purpose must survive the passage from expressed intent to an
      answer, the result must be established under the analytical law and support that apply, and the
      answer must carry no more authority than its grounds warrant.
    </p>

    <div class="criterion">
      <p class="test-label">Conformance test</p>
      <p class="test-line">
        A conforming analytical service must be able to <strong>withhold or qualify analytical
        permission</strong>. Refusal is not an error state; it is the evidence that the permission is
        real.
      </p>
    </div>

    <p class="signpost">
      <a href={paper.href} rel="noopener" target="_blank">{paper.title}</a>
      <span class="meta">Huayin Wang · Version {paper.version} · {longDate(paper.date)} · DOI {paper.doi}</span>
      <span class="role">The category paper. This page is a doorway; the deposit governs.</span>
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .ag-hero { padding-block: clamp(3.5rem, 2rem + 8vw, 7.5rem) var(--ds-turn); }

  .proposition {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: var(--ds-hero);
    line-height: 1.02;
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 22ch;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  .organizing {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: var(--ds-lead);
    line-height: 1.45;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    max-width: 54ch;
    margin: var(--ds-space-3) 0 0;
  }
  .organizing em { font-style: italic; color: var(--ink); }

  .criterion {
    margin-top: var(--ds-space-5);
    padding-top: var(--ds-space-3);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--ds-rule-strong);
  }
  .test-label {
    margin: 0 0 0.55rem;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--ds-meta);
    letter-spacing: 0.09em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }
  .test-line {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: var(--ds-lead);
    line-height: 1.4;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    max-width: 58ch;
  }
  .test-line strong { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 600; }

  .signpost {
    margin: var(--ds-space-4) 0 0;
    padding-top: var(--ds-space-3);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--ds-rule);
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.35rem;
  }
  .signpost a {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: var(--ds-body);
    color: var(--ink);
    text-decoration: none;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--ds-rule-strong);
    padding-bottom: 2px;
    justify-self: start;
  }
  .signpost a:hover { border-bottom-color: var(--ink); }
  .signpost .meta,
  .signpost .role {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--ds-meta);
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  @media (max-width: 46rem) {
    .proposition { max-width: none; }
    .test-line { max-width: none; }
  }
</style>
